{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHtnNTUw4xoFrgyoVjT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted **index 23 (Sb fraction 0.804)** as the best composition. It gave the highest EQE I measured, 0.00453%, but the photoresponse is very weak across the whole Zn–Sb–O line.\n\nI used all 5 EQE measurements. I spread them along the line first, then added points where the first results looked best:\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4 | 0.303 | 0.00273 |\n| 15 | 0.654 | 0.00231 |\n| 19 | 0.753 | −0.00058 (no response) |\n| **23** | **0.804** | **0.00453** |\n| 27 | 0.812 | 0.00443 |\n\n- **Sb-rich end:** indices 23 and 27 are nearly equal and clearly ahead of the other three. The difference between them is small enough that they may be effectively tied.\n- **Not measured:** most of the line, including the 0.33–0.63 range and the gap between 0.30 and 0.65. With so few points, a better composition could be sitting in one of those gaps.\n- **No structure data:** I didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements or the phase and band-gap tools, so I can't say which crystal phase is behind the slightly better Sb-rich results. The low values overall are likely because Zn–Sb oxides have wide band gaps that absorb little of the 2.7 eV light. That is an expectation, not something I checked here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":7826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":427},"output_tokens":480,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2483cd63-09c8-46ac-95e5-d8b72fa9b34d","uuid":"f0d3bd85-6fd1-4f04-8a2c-40ff4b87c402","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:42:23.211Z","request_id":"req_011CfAHtmwu2yHCQQveYP4R1"